{
  "id": "long-log-flags-file-renamed",
  "title": "Integration tests 404 on flag-gated routes: CI still points FEATURE_FLAGS_FILE at the renamed file",
  "description": "PR #518 renames config/flags.yaml and config/flags.test.yaml to config/feature-flags.yaml and config/feature-flags.test.yaml and updates DefaultPath in internal/flags/load.go, but the integration job in .github/workflows/ci.yml still sets FEATURE_FLAGS_FILE: config/flags.test.yaml. flags.Load treats a missing file as 'every flag off', so the API test server never registers the checkout_v2, saved_carts and gift_cards routes and promotions never stack: 26 subtests fail with 'expected status 200, got 404' or 'expected 2 promotions applied, got 1'. The log is a ~4,000-line 'go test -v' run; the 160-line excerpt is filled with the earliest '--- FAIL' windows and the step's tail, and the only line that explains them, 'level=WARN msg=\"feature flags file not found; every flag defaults to off\" path=config/flags.test.yaml', appears once at the top of each failing package's output, far from every error signal. The agent has to search the log (or connect the renamed files in the diff to the workflow env) to find it. A real over-the-size-cap log (20 MB) is not committed; this exercises the same skill. Correct answer: configuration (or code), update FEATURE_FLAGS_FILE in .github/workflows/ci.yml to config/feature-flags.test.yaml. Removing the variable would not work: the production defaults keep checkout_v2 and promo_stacking off.",
  "repo": {
    "owner": "example-org",
    "repo": "checkout-svc"
  },
